course: dictionary
lesson: 12058
title: Clappers: bells, birds and speed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so the words around it tell you which meaning fits. «The bell rang loudly when the clapper hit the side.» Here a clapper is the metal part hanging inside a bell that swings and hits it to make it ring.
explain: «The boy ran like the clappers to catch the bus.» This is not about bells at all. In British, Irish, Australian and New Zealand speech, «like the clappers» means very fast or very hard. The clue is that he is running to catch a bus, so he must be going very fast.
explain: A clapper can also be a device that makes a clapping noise, such as a noisy tool that scares birds away from a field. Film makers use a clapperboard too. When you meet clappers, ask: which meaning fits here? Then try it in the sentence to check.
fact: A clapper is the metal part inside a bell that hits the bell to make it ring.
fact: «Like the clappers» is an informal phrase, used mostly in British, Irish, Australian and New Zealand speech.
fact: «Like the clappers» means very fast or very hard, as in «run like the clappers».
fact: A clapper can also be a device that makes a clapping noise, for example to scare birds.
fact: A clapperboard is used when filming, and it is the board snapped shut at the start of each scene.
exercise: «The clappers inside the church bell swung and hit the metal.» What are the clappers? | Little wooden sticks used to beat a drum | * The metal parts inside a bell that make it ring | The people who ring the bell on Sunday | The ropes that pull the bell
exercise: «She ran like the clappers down the road.» What does like the clappers mean? | * Very fast | Very quietly, on tiptoe | Very slowly, one step at a time | Very sleepy
exercise: «Farmer Jim set up noisy clappers to scare the crows from his corn.» What were the clappers for? | Ringing a church bell | Filming a movie | Running in races | * Scaring birds away
test: «The bell's clapper was broken, so the bell stayed silent.» What is the clapper in this sentence? | A kind of rope for climbing | A loud shout from the crowd | * The part that hits the bell to make it ring | A bird that lives in the church tower
test: «The car sped off like the clappers when the lights turned green.» What does like the clappers suggest? | * Very fast | Very sleepy | Very wet | Very kind
exam: «On the film set, the director snapped the clapperboard before each scene.» Why was the clapperboard used? | To scare birds from the set | * To mark the start of each filmed scene | To ring a bell for lunch | To make the actors run like the clappers
